{
  "id": "projection-neuron",
  "term": "projection neuron",
  "definition": "In this source, a projection neuron is a second-order neuron in the moth antennal lobe pheromone-processing circuit that responds to odorants. Its dendrites and cell body show calcium signals, and the cell-body signal reflects spiking activity; at high odorant concentrations, postsynaptic inhibition can reduce and shorten its response.",
